OneiOS take18, userland/metal/patches/NativeMetal/0009: reflection bindings conform to MTLBinding and its buffer, texture and
threadgroup protocols.
Upstream: Droid-VM/NativeMetal 56044ae (wip/hackintosh, lateautumn233, 2026-11-13), verbatim (README hunk left out).
What: the legacy argument wrapper declares MTLBinding, and buffer, texture and threadgroup arguments are made from
subclasses that conform to MTLBufferBinding, MTLTextureBinding and MTLThreadgroupBinding.
Why: correctness. VFX checks the protocol before it reads a binding's getters: its material reflection objects were
refused and particle material slot 2 stayed unbound (upstream: the Weather app's particles).
Switch: none (correctness fix). Removable: yes (ONEIOS_METAL_SKIP=reflection-binding-protocols); 0010 is left out with it.

